9:The canonical JSON (`ExtractionOutput`, `IncrementalUpdate`, the session index) carries `schemaVersion` (ADR 0017); `SCHEMA_VERSION` in `crates/core/src/types/output.rs` is the one definition, and `schema.rs` requires it. Version 1 is the shape ADR 0009 describes. Version 2 (ADR 0018) writes a component's `props` as prop set ids, and an inheritance layer's `omitted` and a diagnostic's `affects` as name list ids, with `propSets` and `nameLists` tables beside `props`. Version 3 adds `optional` and `rest` to a function type's parameters, written only when true, and lists a rest parameter as the last parameter. OXC keeps `...rest` apart from the other parameters and the extractor read only the others, so `(...args: any[]) => void` printed as `() => void` and `(a?: string) => void` as `(a: string) => void`; a caller reading the signature believed an argument was required or that none were accepted. It is a bump, not an addition a reader can ignore: a version 2 reader would show `...args: any[]` as a required parameter named `args`. The Vite plugin and the Storybook addon read version 3 only, and an old parse cache is discarded once. `raw_string` prints `a?: T` and `...a: T[]` as RDT does, TOON prints `T?` and `...T`, and `structural_hash` includes both flags. The TypeScript 7.1 backend does not set them: `crates/semantic/src/convert.rs` builds every parameter as required. Not carried yet, and best landed together as one more bump: `readonly` (the extractor peels it from `readonly string[]` on purpose; carrying it needs a flag on `PropType::Array` and `Tuple`, their collected forms, the union normalizer, the evaluator's assignability and every printer) and `RefObject` (`resolver/react.rs` maps `Ref`, `RefObject`, `ForwardedRef`, `MutableRefObject`, `RefCallback` and `LegacyRef` to one `PropType::Ref { element }`).

